Measures pages' CPU and memory for freezing only while Battery Saver is on (#686). Chrome's
FreezingPolicy starts its resource usage query as it's made and repeats it each minute for as long
as the browser runs, but only Battery Saver lets a CPU measurement freeze a page, and the memory
measurement only discards frozen pages whose memory grows. So an idle browser off Battery Saver
woke each minute for nothing. The query now starts as Battery Saver turns on and ends as it turns
off; a page CPU-heavy before it turned on freezes after the first minute's measurement rather than
at once.

